"""Script part 7: script_module.cpp (C_ScriptModule's remembered, registered and turning frames, Update, Tick, the
script list, the mission's start, stop and restart, AssignScript, the pause sounds, the cutscenes, the saved values, the
net messages) against the original's.

Run: on script/build_mod.bat, HD2_MOD_QUICK=1 (8,000 cases, about 11 s); MUT_EXTRA_SRCS original_exe.cpp and
mod_calls.s, MUT_LDFLAGS -Wl,--image-base=0x20000000; MUT_PASS "mod_diff: .*, N checks, 0 failures". Prefix N, then
the line.

Result (2026-11-23): 540 mutants, 42 not building; 468 of the 498 building killed. The first run left 39: the humans'
scripted controllers' script was not compared (N 585, 586, 602, 612), the rotations never landed exactly on their angle
(N 233), the input delay never ran out exactly or started at 1 (N 515). Survivors:
- Frees (N 138, 363, 395, 411, 441, 509: leaks); RestoreAnimatedModel's first loop and clear (N 363, 364: the call
  before always empties the list); the name buffers a byte larger or smaller (N 288, 293).
- Never run in the test: the constructor's message bits (N 268: a static object's); a line of the dedicated server's
  build (N 653).
- RotateFrame's padding (N 216: never read); a zero angle taken as negative (N 231: a turn by -0, the same matrix).
- LoadScriptList's loop test (N 283: a failed Descend ends it as well; the files have no stray byte) and its closing
  Ascend and Close (N 302, 303: the chunk's destructor closes it).
- StartMission's first clear of the fake cutscene flag (N 336, 347: each covers the other).
- The remembered frame's new parent (N 388: the test's model reload keeps the same frames, so the parent found is the
  old one).
- RestartMission's flag (N 475: read only by C_Script::Advance, in Tick) and its client calls (N 477, 478, 487, 488:
  StopMission and StartMission without the server return at once).
"""
